# Caddyfile — reverse proxy in front of Vlms.Web's Kestrel process, with automatic HTTPS via
# Let's Encrypt. docs/adr/0005-hosting-pivot-self-hosted-vps-postgresql.md ("Kestrel behind Caddy,
# automatic HTTPS via Let's Encrypt"). STATE.md hosting-pivot item 6.
#
# The site is www.varangians.co.uk (adr/0005 amendment, Philip 12/10/2026); the bare domain
# redirects to it. vlms-web.service's AllowedHosts and App__PublicBaseUrl name the same host —
# change all three together.
#
# Automatic HTTPS syntax verified against Caddy's own current documentation
# (caddyserver.com/docs/quick-starts/reverse-proxy, caddyserver.com/docs/automatic-https) rather
# than assumed: a bare site-address label followed by a directive is genuinely sufficient — "Caddy
# will serve your proxy over HTTPS automatically and by default if it knows the hostname (domain
# name)"; for any hostname other than localhost, Caddy obtains a publicly-trusted certificate
# (Let's Encrypt by default) and manages renewal itself. No separate certbot/acme.sh
# install/cron/renewal-hook is needed or wired here — that whole mechanism is what choosing Caddy
# over nginx/Apache buys this deployment, per the ADR.
#
# Preconditions for the ACME challenge to succeed (not this file's job to satisfy, but real and
# worth stating plainly rather than assuming they'll just work): DNS for the real domain must
# already point at this VPS's public IP, and ports 80 and 443 must be reachable from the public
# internet (Caddy uses 80 for the HTTP-01 challenge / HTTP->HTTPS redirect, 443 for TLS-ALPN and the
# actual site) — a VPS firewall (ufw, cloud provider security group, etc.) must allow both before
# first run, or certificate issuance will fail.
#
# Debian/Ubuntu package install (caddyserver.com/docs/install) sets Caddy up as its own systemd
# service ("caddy") automatically and reads /etc/caddy/Caddyfile by default — this file is meant to
# be installed there (see deploy/README.md), not run standalone; it is a separate systemd unit from
# vlms-web.service/vlms-jobs.service, not one this repo's own unit files manage.

# Bare domain: permanent redirect to www, keeping the path and query
# (caddyserver.com/docs/caddyfile/directives/redir). Caddy gets a certificate for it too.
varangians.co.uk {
	redir https://www.varangians.co.uk{uri} permanent
}

www.varangians.co.uk {
	# Proxies to Vlms.Web's Kestrel process — must match vlms-web.service's
	# ASPNETCORE_URLS=http://127.0.0.1:5000 exactly; both are this deployment's own convention, not
	# a framework default, so keep them in sync if either changes.
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5000

	# Access logging, per-site (caddyserver.com/docs/caddyfile/directives/log). Caddy rotates by
	# size by default (100 MiB, keeping the 10 most recent, gzip-compressed, up to 90 days) — the
	# roll_* sub-directives are left at their documented defaults rather than overridden, since
	# nothing about this deployment's expected traffic volume (tens of users) calls for a different
	# rotation policy yet.
	log {
		output file /var/log/caddy/vlms-web-access.log
	}
}
